However, the comment suggests that the added element should be equal to the last element in the queue after the operation. Since `peek()` returns the head of the queue, we need to check the last element. We can use the fact that if the queue is full, the last element will be at the index just before `start`. If the queue is not full, the last element will be at `end - 1` (considering wrap-around).

Here is the corrected assert statement:

